WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.680
Hi, welcome back to the at-home retreat.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:19.580
Sometimes I call it "online retreat," 
sometimes I call it "at-home retreat." 
"At-home retreat" sounds more friendly, right?

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:31.620
The picture we have here 
is somebody shooting an arrow.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:39.880
And the name of today's class is called 
"Arrows and factories."

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:48.460
I want to teach you an important 
Tibetan word before we start

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:54.120
called pen che kyi le ('PHEN BYED KYI LAS).

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.840
pen ('PHEN) means "to shoot an arrow" 
or "to throw a spear."

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:12.220
Oftentimes in books about karma, 
you hear about a thing--Stanley knows about it--
called pen che kyi le.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:27.100
And this is the karma that you do now 
which is going to throw your next life. 
It's going to decide what your next life is.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:39.840
So if you're a very good person in this life,

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:48.380
you will make karma which will shoot you 
into the future life as a human again.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:02:01.160
And usually they say there's two karmas called 
pen che kyi le, which is the throwing karma,

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.840
and then there's dzok che kyi le (RDZOGS BYED KYI LAS), 
which means "finishing karma."

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:19.520
And they always compare it in the ancient books to a master painter and his student painters.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:44.160
So the master painter in the old days will take a piece of charcoal and they will sketch...like if you're painting a person, they will sketch all the person.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:03.980
So that's like throwing karma, 
it decided you will be a human being.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:13.520
But what are the details of your new life?

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:19.140
Will you be rich? Will you be poor?

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.180
Will you be tall? Will you be short?

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.100
Will you be a woman? Will you be a man?

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:39.420
Then in the metaphor, the student painters... 
the master says, "Paint this part blue, paint this part yellow, paint this part green."

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:50.480
In Tibetan, that's called dzok che (RDZOGS BYED).

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:59.040
So that's the karma which fills in the details of your life, which is thrown by the throwing karma.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:19.600
Now the reason I mentioned those two, 
is I think I've discussed them before in the lam rim (LAM RIM), 
in this lam rim series.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:29.380
But so far this series has taken ten years,

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:37.140
and to be honest, I don't remember 
what I taught you and what I didn't teach you.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:47.600
But what I want to say today is this is not the throwing karma that I taught you before.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:05:02.520
Before, the throwing karma and the details karma were called pen che kyi le and dzok che kyi le.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:16.020
Now we have a slightly different word, which is 
pen che kyi le and du che kyi le ('DU BYED KYI LAS). 

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:27.060
The first kind of karma is the same-- 
you can think of a spear or an arrow.

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:38.300
But the du che kyi le, 
I don't want you to think of student painters.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:47.340
I want you to think of a factory.

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:53.480
They do a lot of things, 
and then a car comes out of the factory.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:03.180
Let's read the text and then you'll be more comfortable.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:11.300
detar tendrel yenlak chu nyi kyi yewa lekpar ngu sung ne
(DE LTAR RTEN 'BREL YAN LAG BCU GNYIS KYI DBYE BA LEGS PAR NGOS BZUNG NAS).

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:19.200
You really have to get familiar 
with these twelve links of dependence.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:33.020
ngu sung (NGOS BZUNG) means if I say, "What's link number three? What's link number five?" you should be able to immediately say what they are.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:40.100
My teacher made us memorize it over and over...

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:56.500
dangpo marikpa, nyipa du che, sumpa namshe, shipa ming suk chi rik,
ngapa kye che, drukpa rekpa, dunpa tsorwa, gyepa sepa, gupa lenpa,
chupa sipa, chu chikpa kyewa, chu nyipa ga shiy
(DANG PO MA RIG PA, GNYIS PA 'DU BYED, GSUM PA RNAM SHES, BZHI PA MING GZUGS CI RIGS, LNGA PA SKYE MCHED, DRUG PA REG PA, BDUN PA TSOR BA, BRGYAD PA SRED PA, DGU PA LEN PA, BCU PA SRID PA, BCU GCIG PA SKYE BA, BCU GNYIS PA RGA SHI'I)

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:59.260
...you know we had to say it over and over again.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:07.000
Then he would say, "What's that one? What's that one? What's that one?" So, I hope you guys will do that.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:14.020
Now after you know all the twelve links 
like individual friends,

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:21.960
or individual enemies actually,

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:32.060
yang yenlak shir du luk she gu
(YANG YAN LAG BZHIR BSDU LUGS SHES DGOS)--
you should be familiar with how 
these are grouped into groups.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:43.920
And there are four groups. Now if you're studying the Tibetan and you're following the Tibetan,

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:58.420
I want to say, unfortunately, the word in Tibetan, yen lak (YAN LAG), and the word in Sanskrit, anga (aṅga अङ्ग),

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:10.460
they are the same word for the links 
and the same word for the groups.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:22.740
I'm going to use different words 
so you don't get confused.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:26.220
There are four groups of links.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:32.520
The first one is called pen che kyi yenlak ('PHEN BYED KYI YAN LAG)--

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:37.940
that's the "shooting group."

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:45.960
Second is drup che kyi yenlak ('GRUB BYED KYI YAN LAG)-- 
that's the "factory group."

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:56.300
pangpay drebuy yenlak ('PHANGS PA'I 'BRAS BU'I YAN LAG) 
means "what was shot." You can say "the arrow."

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:10.980
Group one is kind of like the archer 
and group three is kind of like the arrow.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:15.980
Group two is like the factory.

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:25.380
Group four, ngunpar druppay drebuy yenlak te 
('MNGON PAR GRUB PA'I 'BRAS BU'I YAN LAG STE), 
is kind of like what the factory puts out.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:31.480
So there we have four groups.

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:39.920
Arrow shooter, car producing factory,

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:47.640
the arrow which you shoot, 
and the car which comes out of the factory.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:58.040
de yang marikpa ni sabun deppapo tabu dang de kun ne langway du che kyi le ni sabun tabu dang
(DE YANG MA RIG PA NI SA BON 'DEBS PA PO LTA BU DANG, DES KUN NAS BSLANG BA'I 'DU BYED KYI LAS NI SA BON LTA BU DANG)

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:03.180
Now if we're going to talk about it in terms of gardening,

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:18.500
then the first thing, misunderstanding, is like the gardener who puts the seed in the ground.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:27.500
And the actions you take 
because you have misunderstanding,

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:35.940
karma, those are like the seed 
that's planted by the gardener.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:46.420
Now the earth where you put the seed

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:55.120
is the first half of link number three, which is awareness.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:06.420
So when you say to your husband, 
"I'm not stupid, you're stupid," which is link number two, 

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:15.900
because you thought to yourself, "I didn't do anything,"

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:20.060
which is link number one. 

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:25.080
I'm not offering him money today.
I lost all my money yesterday.

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:29.260
Then, what's link number three?

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:44.500
It's the mind of the wife in the kitchen at the time that she says, "I'm not stupid, you're stupid," and she hears her own words, and those words are imprinted on her mind.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:12:08.000
We call that: link number three, 
your mind, at the moment of planting.

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:25.940
Now the second half of link number three
is going to be the mind as the seed opens
and goes into the mum's womb.

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:38.360
So, let's consider these links. 
Number one, which is misunderstanding your husband,

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:46.000
and then link number two, which is doing some karma,

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:52.760
and then we can throw in 
the first half of consciousness.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:59.880
Those two and a half links...

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:03.030
che dang sum (PHYED DANG GSUM) in Tibetan.

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:09.500
It means if you added another half you would get three, you see, so that's the Tibetan way to say "two and a half."

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:21.440
These are the archer. These two and a half links 
are the one who shoots the arrow.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:32.780
I put an image here and I drew, 
I think it's a blue cloud, around the shooting links.

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:45.180
Now we'll go back to the text:

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:49.920
sabun la chu lu dru sher gyi kyangpa
(SA BON LA CHU LUD, DROD GSHER GYIS BSKYANGS PA)

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:57.660
Now you take that seed--sabun (SA BON)--and you put on it chu (CHU), which is water, 

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:07.240
and lu (LUD), which is fertilizer, and then dru sher (DROD GSHER) means that you make it kind of wet and warm.

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:18.340
kyangpa (BSKYANGS PA) is an ancient word that means what a mom does to their kid when they feed them and they take care of them.

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:29.040
So kyangpa means these extra things--water, fertilizer, sunlight--they are supporting the seed, they are feeding the seed.

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:46.900
So which of the links are like the water, and the fertilizer, and the sunlight? You know! It's eight and nine.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:59.480
They make the karmic seed ready to give a baby.

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:08.360
In terms of the death process,

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:19.680
we can speak more specifically of the one seed which is going to be activated to shoot your next life.

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:41.200
And we talked about being very careful to make the hospital room comfortable, and to speak quietly, and to remind people of their good deeds.

00:15:55.120 --> 00:16:06.680
So you can explain link eight and link nine in general terms of your whole life. You should do coffee meditation or you should regret the bad things you did.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:35.060
Or you can think of eight and nine more specifically as the last moment of your general awareness of this lifetime before your mind shifts to like, an animal mind.

00:16:45.720 --> 00:17:01.400
When I say at the last moment of your life, your general awareness of this world shifts to animal state of mind, I don't mean you become an animal or you have an animal's mind. I don't mean that.

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:17.020
I mean your mind dies--

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:21.180
99% of your mind dies--

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:31.020
and all that's left, we call it nyuk sem (GNYUG SEMS), nyuk sem.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:42.920
That means like, "primeval mind," 
the mind which you've had for billions of lifetimes.

00:17:48.020 --> 00:17:52.460
And by the way, that's why it's very difficult to remember what happened in your past life.

00:17:57.100 --> 00:18:05.140
You can say 99% of your mind died during that last minute of awareness.

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:20.120
So that seed in the garden 
gets its water and its fertilizer.

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:29.820
By link ten, the seed gets very fat. 

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:35.100
yang si chimay kyeway pungpo pen nge su chepa
(YANG SRID PHYI MA'I SKYE BA'I PHUNG 
PO 'PHEN NGES SU BYED PA)

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:42.160
And it makes it certain that that seed 
is going to throw a new life.

00:18:46.860 --> 00:18:58.340
So therefore links eight, nine, and ten-- 
I like to call them factory links--

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:04.360
they are producing your new body and your new mind.

00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:13.160
By link ten, the new body and mind 
are almost ready for shipping.

00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:26.080
So again, I showed an image here 
of links eight, nine, and ten.

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:36.920
And by the way, the links are equal to the old clocks... like one, two, three, four, five... So eight, nine, and ten are going to be where eight, nine, and ten o'clock are.

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:58.120
So we finished the shooting links,

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:05.260
and we finished the factory, 
which is getting your new body and mind ready.

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:10.840
Now let's go back to the text.

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:17.220
sabun gyi nyu gu kyepa shin kye si du nying tsam jorwa ni
(SA BON GYI MYU GU SKYES PA BZHIN SKYE SRID DU NYING MTSAMS SBYOR BA NI)

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:24.160
So let's go to the moment that the seed splits open 
and the sprout comes out.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:38.500
This is like the production that comes out of the factory, and that's link number eleven, which is your rebirth.

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:46.940
Now there's going to be another production link, 
but we'll come to it later.

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:57.080
So, if the factory is the seed already wet and fertilized,

00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:09.160
then the production coming out of the factory--the first part of that production--is your rebirth.

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:19.420
And in the image here you see link number eleven, 
and I've added twelve,

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:29.540
because that's going to be another production, 
but in the text it's coming a little bit later.

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:44.360
gong du shepa tar gyi dre du kyi namshe dang ming suk chi rikpay tendrel, kye che, rekpa, tsorwa te tendrel che dang nga ni pangpay drebuy
(GONG DU BSHAD PA LTAR GYI 'BRAS DUS KYI RNAM SHES DANG MING GZUGS CI RIGS PA'I RTEN 'BREL, SKYE MCHED, REG PA, TSOR BA STE RTEN 'BREL PHYED DANG LNGA NI 'PHANGS PA'I 'BRAS BU'I)

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:47.900
So what's the arrow that gets shot?

00:21:50.100 --> 00:21:59.860
Who's the shooter? Do you remember? 
Oh, it's: "I misunderstood my husband,  
then I yelled at my husband."

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:05.280
Then the first half of link number three, my mind, 
is where where the seed is planted.

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:14.280
Now what's the arrow that gets shot?

00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:26.120
He lists it here: the second half of your third link, which is the mind entering in the womb.

00:22:27.040 --> 00:22:32.500
Then the two guys in the boat-- 
your mind and your body inside your mother's womb.

00:22:37.340 --> 00:22:40.560
And then your sense organs.

00:22:40.980 --> 00:22:47.320
Then the contact of your mind with the outside world because of those organs.

00:22:50.960 --> 00:22:58.880
And in the feelings you have about that contact-- 
"that food stinks," "that food smells good."

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:07.320
Actually, it should be, "I like that smell" 
or "I don't like that smell."

00:23:10.360 --> 00:23:18.500
So four and a half of the links 
are the arrow which is thrown.

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:25.940
In Tibetan, they're called "result links which are thrown."

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:38.220
Ok, one more small piece here. 
ga shi chi rikpay tendrel ni (RGA SHI CI RIGS PA'I RTEN 'BREL NI)--
now, let's talk about link number twelve.

00:23:39.840 --> 00:23:45.480
For twenty dollars, what's the technical name?

00:23:45.960 --> 00:23:50.980
[Stanley: death, maybe with aging]

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:57.780
Death with maybe aging.

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:05.640
Twenty dollars. My banker is over there. Twenty dollars for your partner.

00:24:06.320 --> 00:24:12.060
So now we're talking about...

00:24:13.040 --> 00:24:16.120
I'm sorry... I got distracted...

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:20.420
This link of death and maybe aging,

00:24:23.040 --> 00:24:30.360
that's another production link-- 
we promised you one more production link right? 
The car that came out of the factory...

00:24:34.800 --> 00:24:39.460
So that whole experience of getting old and dying

00:24:42.040 --> 00:24:50.020
is a car which is produced in the factory of 
links eight, nine, and ten, which is the fat seed.

00:24:54.660 --> 00:25:00.560
That's the most boring class 
I gave you in this group. I think so.

00:25:04.280 --> 00:25:10.980
And this is when my friends say, "Geshe-la, can you teach something that we can really use?"

00:25:15.640 --> 00:25:21.240
And I apologize that I don't always 
show you how to use it.

00:25:26.600 --> 00:25:30.840
There's not one word of Dharma that you cannot use,

00:25:35.300 --> 00:25:44.080
and the older you get, the more you appreciate all the things that people have taught you, which I have many.

00:25:51.800 --> 00:25:56.020
But because in these last two days of classes,

00:25:58.580 --> 00:26:04.680
we talked about the sections of the Wheel of Life 
that kind of hang together,

00:26:10.720 --> 00:26:15.940
we are now in a position 
to answer an important question:

00:26:19.880 --> 00:26:25.020
how many lives are going on in one wheel?

00:26:27.440 --> 00:26:32.020
And if you want to know that, 
come back for a session eighteen.

00:26:34.660 --> 00:26:39.460
Thank you Stanley for translating so happily.

